========================================================================
  Observation: Qwen-7B vs Qwen-3B Comparison (§IX)
========================================================================
  Qwen-7B produces higher-quality handoffs → gate score distribution shifts right
  → tau* must be set higher (0.7972 vs 0.695) to maintain same recall
  AUROC: 0.8619 (7B) > 0.8341 (3B), confirming better signal quality with larger model
  
  Clean-task false-positive rate: 7B=8.7%, 3B=11.4%, Primary=14.9%
  → Larger models are harder to gate (fewer false positives) because their handoffs
    are more informative even when corrupted.

  Paper claim (§IX): "The gate generalizes to Qwen-2.5-Coder-7B with AUROC 0.862,
  demonstrating backbone-agnostic feature utility."

